{
 "meta": {
  "protocol": "tr_lib.tapes(n), 300 random tapes, n in [512, 1024, 2048]",
  "model": "BTHM-C_4: the oracle answers the visit count of the quadruple (ell, r, L, R) mod 4 (colour 0 = first visit, 1 = second, 2 = third, 3 = fourth); the rule reads the colour; the repair (cut_engine mode 4) fires when the colour returns to 0, i.e. on the fifth visit, so visits 2-4 are played by the rule.  The oracle read is free and takes no step.",
  "design": "the four colour-variants of a base rule: colour 0 = the base rule; colour 1 = the mirror of the move (LPLUS<->RMINUS, LMINUS<->RPLUS; the three trims and halt fixed); colour 2 = the cut side swapped (CUTL<->CUTR); colour 3 = both.  A move that would leave the region is replaced by a cut -- on the side the move would leave for colours 0 and 1, on the opposite side for colours 2 and 3; the double cut used when the window fills the region is kept for every colour.  The repair reads the side off the colour-0 (base) table, exactly as cut_engine mode 4.",
  "charge": "pcr_lib INC accounting in both models; a repair pays the re-span abs(y-L)+abs(x-R_) plus the head re-read; the colour is free.",
  "cap": "40 n^2 + 100, unchanged",
  "engines": "probe_colour/col_engine.py (mode 5) on the walk of probe_trim/cut_engine.py; colour-blind side taken from probe_trim/cut_cells.json and probe_trim/cut_<rule>_<n>.json as stored, never recomputed.",
  "rungs": "(0.5, 1, 1.5, 2, 2.9, 3), tolerance 0.15",
  "tail_criterion": "mean and maximum of the same order: the geometric mean G, the mean e and the max g of the reads over all 300 tapes satisfy 1/3 <= G/e (i.e. e/G <= 3) and g/e <= 3.  A heavy tail violates one or both."
 },
